From 542c48f2d6c84d0cdb64769e5c8ff4932ed0624f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cody Ho <codyho@stanford.edu>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 21:54:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: pipeline M4 firmware submissions and retire
 completions asynchronously

Replace the one-command hardware wait with a 16-command publication window,
per-Work stamps and context leases, and firmware barriers for queue ordering.
Keep compute resource-table views private until VM destruction, issue the full
CDM cache barrier needed for dependent writes, and echo TVB subpipe/halt counters.
Preserve actual completion fences, independent-queue progress and teardown
ownership; detect lack of retirement progress instead of elapsed queue time.

Validated on the physical M4 with 32 dependent compute SUBMITs, 16 queued
partial renders, mixed render/compute, delayed fences/timestamps, local-indirect
geometry and targeted UAPI/lifetime checks. Actual Rust memory/cursor checks
pass; the final kernel build is warning-free.

(cherry picked from commit c9a25ac00dac0324f892c00221157bd7453633f2)
